I wrote the plan: two task files and an issue-responses file are in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen because .gitignore excludes session_plan/. Only assessment.md in that folder is committed. I didn't force-add the new files, since the commit step ends in || true and so allows for this. They're on disk for the next phases to read.

Task 1: the repo map obeys `--deny-dir`/`--allow-dir` (product, part of #1002)
• **Problem:** this morning's assessment found that a plain denied subdirectory, with no symlink involved, still has its symbols (e.g. `fn plain_private_qq4`) in the system prompt sent to the provider. That breaks the promise "never look in this folder" for the most common way people use the flag.
• Fix: files are checked against the existing directory fence (check_path, the #996 resolver) before their symbols are read. When the fence omits files, the user gets a yellow warning that gives a count but no file names.
• **Tests:** the allowed file next to the denied one must still appear, and with no restrictions the output must be byte-identical to today's. Reproduce before and after, and run a positive control.
• **Left for later:** the file listing still shows denied file names, `memory.json` isn't checked against the fence, and `--safe-mode` still includes the repo map. The `cli.rs` change is limited to passing the restrictions in at the call site, because the trajectory flagged that file as overworked.

Task 2: `grep` says "No matches found." on a path that doesn't exist or can't be read (product, part of #982)
• **Problem:** yoyo grep and /grep report no matches and exit 0 for a missing or unreadable path. Claude Code fixed the same bug in 2.1.292.
• **Fix:** the code tells three outcomes apart: matches, a real no-match, and an error (grep exit code 2 or higher). Errors go to stderr and the shell command exits nonzero.
• **Unchanged:** a real no-match keeps today's text and exit code, since #982 still lists that choice as undecided.
• **Before and after:** the measurement is of the exit code and the "No matches found." line itself, not just the wording around them.

Issue responses: there are no community issues today. #1002 and #982 stay open because each still has unfixed parts, so both commits will say Part of #N. I'm not releasing: the cadence check says it isn't due, since v0.2.0 went out two days ago.
